<%# The auth sheet's first frame (story 0017 Release 2). No layout.

    ASWebAuthenticationSession can only open a URL, and OmniAuth's request phase
    is POST-only — `shared/_auto_submit_auth_form` (story 0021) is what turns
    the one into the other; this file only supplies the URL.

    `native=1` rides the QUERY STRING, not a hidden field, and that is not a
    style choice. OmniAuth's request phase stashes `request.GET` — only the
    query — into the session as `omniauth.params`, and hands that back on the
    callback. A field in the POST body is never seen again, so the callback
    could not tell the sheet's flow from a browser's. %>
<%= render "shared/auto_submit_auth_form", url: "/auth/#{@provider}?native=1" %>
